(7671812, 1252637, 86447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GolferDDS:</b></div><hr/><i> This was my favorite of the challenge. I cant imagine why it didnt score higher. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think it''s the "washed out" look that hurt your score.<br/> <br/>It''s a great image.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by GolferDDS: This was my favorite of the challenge. I cant imagine why it didnt score higher.   I think it''s the "washed out" look that hurt your score. It''s a great image. ', '2020-08-07 17:24:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7671813, 1252544, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GolferDDS:</b></div><hr/><i> I like your nonchalance. You walk into a store, take a picture, submit it in a contest and get a ribbon!  My grandmother used to have these out when I was a child. Funny how one remembers these things....</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes, this is often my photo-taking strategy as well (minus the ribbon-winning part!)<br/> <br/>When  I was in elementary school my best friend''s dad was the northern California importer-distributor for a variety of foreign candy/specialty items -- I was introduced to "good" chocolate by the third grade or so ...<br/> <br/>I don''t remember the neon colors -- mostly the ones like this I had were a more pastel white and pink, possibly with coconut between the licorice layers.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on the yellow.</td>', 'Originally posted by GolferDDS: I like your nonchalance. You walk into a store, take a picture, submit it in a contest and get a ribbon!  My grandmother used to have these out when I was a child. Funny how one remembers these things.... Yes, this is often my photo-taking strategy as well (minus the ribbon-winning part!) When  I was in elementary school my best friend''s dad was the northern California importer-distributor for a variety of foreign candy/specialty items -- I was introduced to "good" chocolate by the third grade or so ... I don''t remember the neon colors -- mostly the ones like this I had were a more pastel white and pink, possibly with coconut between the licorice layers. Congratulations on the yellow.', '2020-08-07 17:33:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7671814, 1252544, 86447, '<td valign="top">You could take a photo of a blank wall and ribbon, Anita!<br/> <br/>Congratulations!<br/></td>', 'You could take a photo of a blank wall and ribbon, Anita! Congratulations!', '2020-08-07 17:49:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7671815, 1252637, 98565, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GolferDDS:</b></div><hr/><i> This was my favorite of the challenge. I cant imagine why it didnt score higher. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think it''s the "washed out" look that hurt your score.<br/> <br/>It''s a great image. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you all for your lovely comments<br/>Yes, Lydia, I did overexpose on purpose, I thought it fitted the sweet look and took emphasis away from the girl.<br/>Because that was my main concern: that voters would stick strictly to the word "candy" and not accept a model in the shot.<br/> <br/>However - I''m happy with this result.<br/>And my "Zuckerschnecke" likes it too</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: Originally posted by GolferDDS: This was my favorite of the challenge. I cant imagine why it didnt score higher.   I think it''s the "washed out" look that hurt your score. It''s a great image.   Thank you all for your lovely commentsYes, Lydia, I did overexpose on purpose, I thought it fitted the sweet look and took emphasis away from the girl.Because that was my main concern: that voters would stick strictly to the word "candy" and not accept a model in the shot. However - I''m happy with this result.And my "Zuckerschnecke" likes it too', '2020-08-07 17:56:46.000000', NULL, 0),
